# Mosquitto ACL — security audit 2026-08-19 Val 1.5.
# Trusted server-side services (all drivers, Node-RED, pv-stack-ui) share
# the `admin` user and keep full access — tightening them is a separate,
# higher-risk effort with no immediate security gain.
user admin
topic readwrite #
# $SYS/# is NOT covered by the '#' wildcard in mosquitto — it needs an
# explicit grant. The broker's Docker healthcheck subscribes to
# $SYS/broker/uptime as admin; without this it times out and the
# container reads 'unhealthy' (regression fixed 2026-08-19).
topic read $SYS/#

# seplos-modbus driver: full access preserved (publishes seplos/# +
# 541 homeassistant/# discovery topics; scoping it would break HA).
user seplos
topic readwrite #

# bridge_ro — the ONLY component that relays broker data to browsers
# (mqtt-bridge WS fan-out). Read-only, and DENIED the credential-bearing
# config namespace at the broker level (defense in depth behind the
# bridge's own ingress deny-list). The bridge never publishes.
user bridge_ro
topic read #
topic deny pv-stack/config/#

# mbg-node — the account baked into ESP node firmware (multi-bus-gateway-esphome,
# 2026-10-10). A board's flash can be read by whoever holds it, so this account
# reaches ONLY the nodes' own namespace: announcements now, node state and
# commands later. Never # — that would hand the whole stack (Victron control
# included) to anyone with a node in hand.
# A node only says who it is and answers; it reads its commands and cannot
# write any — so a board in someone's hands cannot command the others.
user mbg-node
topic write mbg/nodes/+/announce
topic write mbg/nodes/+/event
topic read mbg/nodes/+/cmd
# a configured node (the wizard's YAML, topic_prefix mbg/nodes/<mac>):
# online/offline, its entities' states out, their commands in — ESPHome's
# own <prefix>/<component>/<object_id>/{state,command}
topic write mbg/nodes/+/status
topic write mbg/nodes/+/+/+/state
topic read mbg/nodes/+/+/+/command
# the node's own log (warnings by default; more for a while on request, 2026-10-11)
topic write mbg/nodes/+/log

# EMS containers (pv-stack-ems, audit 2026-10-22 A6): read everything, write
# only their own namespace. One writer per actuator: W/# and
# pv/inverters/+/cmd/# stay with Node-RED (admin) — a user with rules of its
# own is denied every topic not listed here.
user ems-io
topic read #
topic write ems/v1/#
# ADR-0015 §3 (2026-10-25): ems-io's writes are the gateway's commands on the GX
# device — one topic family, nothing else of mbg/#. The gateway guards, verifies
# and arms the dead-man; the command must also be enabled on the device there.
topic write mbg/devices/victron-gx/cmd/#
user ems-control
topic read #
topic write ems/v1/#
user ems-app
topic read #
topic write ems/v1/#
